    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the domains already separate — and where they do not",
      "prov:value": "An early version of this page answered by matching filenames. That is a lower\nbound by construction — it finds `lean-build-bg.sh` and misses a Lean special\ncase inside a generic validator — so it has been replaced by a real import-graph\npartition, `bun run cat check:partition`\n(`scripts/repo-partition.ts`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "filename heuristic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The partition",
      "prov:value": "by the bean `dh4f` question:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dh4f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The wrong-direction edges — Phase I's worklist",
      "prov:value": "> **It is not a complete count over the checkout, and this passage read as if it\n> were until 2026-09-30 (bean `p11x`).** `check:partition`'s root is **one\n> instance**, so \"every module is classified\" means every module under that\n> instance. Imports between instances that already exist side by side are\n> outside the scan entirely, and `bf5l` measured one that this tool reports as\n> `0` while `kg:detangle` reports it as `1`. The cross-instance axis is\n> `bun run cat kg:detangle:direction`, blocking in CI since the owner's Option 2\n> ruling. The table below is the **within-instance** worklist.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p11x",
        "bean bf5l",
        "2026-09-30",
        "Option 2"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The wrong-direction edges — Phase I's worklist",
      "prov:value": "**On the count's history.** The first run reported 33 cross-edges with 135\nmodules unassigned; classifying the test material and the standalone MCP server\ntook it to 41; triaging the last 27 took it to 45. **Classifying more modules\nfinds more violations, not fewer.** The number only stopped moving because the\nunassigned column reached zero — which is why that column, not the edge count,\nis the one to check first when re-running this.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "33 → 41 → 45 → 46"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The wrong-direction edges — Phase I's worklist",
      "prov:value": "**It then went to 46 without anyone touching a boundary.** Merging ten commits\nfrom `main` brought five new modules — the CRDM stakeholder-map tooling and the\nBPMN reference check, all harness — and one of them imports the content model.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "46 edges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What is not wired",
      "prov:value": "| `resolveSkillDirs` | **0** |\n| `resolveTranslationDirs` | **0** |\n| `resolveContentDirs` | *does not exist* |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "resolveSkillDirs 0 callers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the model used to rule out — resolved 2026-09-18",
      "prov:value": "The docstring was, until this change, explicit that two things are **never**\nresolved from a dependency: schemas, and MCP tools — \"always from the root\nfolio-assistant\". For a single-platform world that was a reasonable\nsimplification.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/current-state.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the model used to rule out — resolved 2026-09-18",
      "prov:value": "**The same docstring was also optimistic in the other direction**, and that\nhalf is not fixed, only correctly reported.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "docstring table"
      ]
    },
    {
